    "body": "## Security impact\n\nThe proposal endpoints still resolved jobs globally before proving that the caller was allowed to observe that resource. This created several existence/lifecycle oracles and, on owner-only acceptance paths, allowed an unrelated caller to reach job mode/status checks before the request was scoped to the job owner.\n\nThe highest-sensitivity paths are acceptance funding and acceptance itself because they sit directly in front of escrow and wallet logic. A non-owner must be rejected before proposal, held-escrow or wallet reads, while the true requester must retain the existing lifecycle and funding behavior.\n\n## Fix\n\n- scope proposal submission directly to a pessimistically locked `OPEN + PROPOSALS` job, so missing, terminal and `INSTANT` jobs are not materialized by the submission path;\n- scope acceptance-funding reads to `job.createdBy == requester` before assignment-mode, lifecycle, proposal, escrow or wallet access;\n- scope proposal acceptance to a pessimistically locked requester-owned job before proposal or escrow mutation;\n- preserve the established neutral `403` contract for non-owners on acceptance-funding/acceptance, including nonexistent job IDs;\n- preserve useful lifecycle conflicts for the actual requester after ownership is established;\n- check proposal ownership before taking the existing job lock on withdrawal, while preserving the same job lock and lifecycle validation for a legitimate proposer;\n- preserve proposal history: the requester can still list all proposals after a job becomes terminal, and a proposer can still read their own proposal; an unrelated viewer only sees an empty list for a currently public `OPEN + PROPOSALS` job and gets not-found once it is private/terminal.\n\nNo escrow arithmetic, wallet contribution calculation, Stripe minimum, transaction ordering, assignment mutation order, proposal rejection logic, tracking initialization or notification semantics are changed.\n\n## Tests\n\nFocused service regressions prove that:\n- unavailable/instant jobs are rejected by the scoped submission lookup without the legacy global lock;\n- terminal proposal jobs are hidden from unrelated list viewers while owner/proposer history remains available;\n- non-owner funding is rejected before proposal, escrow and wallet reads;\n- true owners receive lifecycle conflicts only after owner scoping;\n- non-owner acceptance is rejected before proposal or escrow mutation;\n- withdrawal rejects non-owners before taking a job lock, while legitimate withdrawal retains the existing lock/lifecycle path;\n- existing higher-proposal escrow adjustment and rollback behavior remains covered.\n\nThe runtime proposal-funding smoke additionally requires the same `403` for an outsider querying/accepting an existing job and a nonexistent job, then runs the unchanged owner funding, rollback and exact-delta escrow acceptance scenario.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after all relevant checks on the exact PR head are green. Revalidate the PR head and current `master` immediately before merge, merge with a merge commit using the exact checked head SHA, then verify the resulting merge parents and all post-merge workflows before starting another slice.",
